<title>GREECE: Greek Jan-April C/A deficit up 21.3pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Greek Jan-April C/A deficit up 21.3pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's current account deficit rose 21.3 percent year-on-year to $2.28 billion in the first four months of 1997 and the trade deficit widened 7.2 percent year-on-year to $6.33 billion, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Current account figures provided by the Bank of Greece</p>
<p>   (figures in $million)   Jan-April 97     Jan-April 96</p>
<p>   Current account	    -2,287	    -1,885</p>
<p>   Trade   balance	    -6,332	    -5,909</p>
<p>   Invisibles		    4,045	     4,024</p>
<p>   Exports fob		   1,700	     1,957</p>
<p>   Imports cif		   8,032	     7,866</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
